WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.890
- Today I have a very special guest

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.150
on the Wednesday Checkup.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.510
Oh, it's the slobbery Bear.

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:08.040
Today we're sharing a story all about him.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.963
I'm ready, Bear are you ready?

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.543
He's ready, be woo!

00:00:12.543 --> 00:00:15.210
(relaxed music)

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.500
I wanna start off by
telling you right away,

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.820
little Bear was diagnosed
with Lyme disease.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.170
(sad music)

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.020
Don't worry, he's fine, this
story has a happy ending.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.150
I just wanna tell you about the process.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.700
How did Bear get diagnosed
with Lyme Disease?

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:32.970
What I did to treat it.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.900
I enrolled Bear in a
training program to get him

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.010
to be hospital certified as a therapy dog,

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.860
because I think Bear is so doofy and cute,

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.120
he can bring a lot of happiness and joy

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.500
to those who are unfortunately spending

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.730
some significant amount
of time in the hospital.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.310
When bear came back from training,

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:54.810
he was due for his annual
physical exam, some vaccinations.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.990
I also needed a refill of
his heartworm medication.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.650
This is a monthly tab
that you give to dogs

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.960
to prevent parasitic heart disease.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.580
Before most vets will give
the first prescription

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.420
of heartworm medication,
they'll do a rapid test

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.290
to confirm the dog actively
doesn't have that illness.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:13.090
Because if they do, they
need to get treated for it

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.990
before getting put on a preventive dosage.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.650
What I didn't know was that
when they did the rapid test,

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:20.510
it also included a rapid
test for Lyme disease.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:22.870
When the vet tech came back, they tell me

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:24.850
that Bear's positive for Lyme disease.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.070
Bear is completely asymptomatic.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:30.150
No joint issues, no
joint pain, no limping,

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.760
he's happy-go-lucky, eating
well, pooping well, peeing well,

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.270
everything was great, so it's
probably a false positive.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:38.370
But, 24 hours later, a new vet calls me

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.600
and says, "He is positive
for Lyme disease."

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.090
When I asked some follow-up questions,

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.120
I wasn't quite happy with
the responses I was getting.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.450
The vet wasn't certain about
what the test was looking for.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.600
Was it antigen, viral load, antibodies?

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.270
He didn't have much
experience with Lyme disease,

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.760
so I said, thank you,
I'll make my own decision

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.190
and I'll follow up with the office.

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:00.260
I know when it comes to Lyme disease,

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.970
in humans it can be a
very controversial topic.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.860
I didn't know how controversial
it was in animals.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:08.240
Lyme disease is a tick-borne illness

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:11.220
that can be largely
prevented by having proper

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.560
tick prevention methods in action.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.880
Bear loves to run around in grass.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:19.270
He grew up in upstate New York,
which is a haven for ticks.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:21.740
He has very thick, dense, brown fur,

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.720
so it's near impossible to see

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.760
if he has a tick on him to remove it.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.310
In treating Lyme disease in humans,

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.390
I know the mainstay of
treatment is antibiotics,

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.530
however, I didn't wanna subject Bear

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.870
to antibiotics unnecessarily.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.040
So I decided to jump into the research

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.340
and see what I found when
it comes to treating dogs

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:41.710
who weren't showing symptoms,

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:43.810
to see if it's even
worthwhile to treat them.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.920
And what I found really surprised me.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.000
I'm not a vet.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.410
I don't pretend to be a vet.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.520
I'm not giving you advice

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.110
on what you should do with your dog.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:54.570
It's simply me describing
to you what I found

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.060
in quality veterinary literature.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.460
In 2006, the American College

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:02.750
of Veterinary Internal
Medicine, published a consensus

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.078
of what doctors, vets specifically,

00:03:05.078 --> 00:03:08.430
thought about treating
dogs with Lyme disease.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.860
They did an update to this in 2018,

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.580
which is great, considering
Bear was just diagnosed

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.390
with Lyme disease in 2019.

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:17.447
This is what it states, verbatim.

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:19.707
"The topic is still controversial.

00:03:19.707 --> 00:03:23.447
"Four out of six doctors
do not routinely recommend

00:03:23.447 --> 00:03:24.950
"treatments for such dogs."

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:28.010
The majority of vets on this
Internal Medicine Committee,

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:31.800
recommend against treating
dogs with antibiotics

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.140
that just solely have a
positive Lyme disease test,

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:36.790
but don't show any other symptoms,

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.320
and their urine studies are normal.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:39.767
The reason why they say that,

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:42.547
"It promotes overuse of antibiotics.

00:03:42.547 --> 00:03:45.447
"There's no data proving that
treatment of healthy dogs

00:03:45.447 --> 00:03:48.270
"is associated with
decreased risk of illness."

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:49.103
Very important.

00:03:49.103 --> 00:03:52.087
"Lyme may not be cleared from
all tissues with treatment.

00:03:52.087 --> 00:03:55.730
"Reinfection may commonly occur
in dogs in endemic areas."

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.890
Now this consensus is very important.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:59.820
I was able to make the
decision to hold off

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.500
on treating Bear for Lyme disease.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.870
However, fast forward a few weeks later,

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:07.700
Bear started limping and he
started getting arthraglias,

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.530
which means pain in his joints.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.560
So I knew it was time to start
treating his Lyme disease,

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.370
because he was starting
to get affected by it

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.560
and showing symptoms.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.640
So I went to the vet,
picked up the prescription

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:21.140
for doxycycline, which is
the antibiotic of choice

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:22.620
in treating Lyme disease,

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.190
and it's a very long course,

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.790
it's actually a 30 day
course of antibiotics.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.000
Now, when you're giving
a dog, or even a human

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.739
such a long course of antibiotics,

00:04:30.739 --> 00:04:33.160
I think it's wise to
get them on a probiotic

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.410
at the same time, so you're not completely

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:37.530
destroying the bacteria
that's found in our gut,

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:38.690
or in the animal's gut.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.580
And Bear did actually really
well with the doxycycline.

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.010
He didn't have any side effects.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:45.310
I was happy that I was
able to get a treatment,

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.190
but not unnecessary treatment.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:50.170
It's always good to become more informed

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:52.110
on the illness that you or your animal's

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:54.950
been diagnosed with, and
then bring that information

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:58.133
to the doctor, or to another
doctor for a second opinion.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.800
It's been two months since
we finished the antibiotics.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:02.920
Bear's doing great.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.430
He's happy, we're back in training mode.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.700
He asked if we could open
some packages on camera

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.309
for a Mail Time segment.

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.840
- Hi mailman!
(screaming)

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:11.890
- What do you think about it?

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:12.970
Should we do it?

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:14.250
Should we do Mail Time?

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.570
Doesn't this face look like a face

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:16.403
that wants to do Mail Time?

00:05:16.403 --> 00:05:17.236
Mail Time.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.740
All right Bear, so we're
gonna open some packages.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.580
And I promise I'll give you
whatever was yours, okay?

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:24.513
It's a letter, and,

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.620
a little badge, oh it's
a little heart badge,

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.310
look at that.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.010
Look how cute, Bear (laughs)
that's not for you to eat.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:34.920
Thank you so much, someone from the UK.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.036
Bear this is the one with your
name on it, are you ready?

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:39.199
Do, do, do, do, do, do, do.

00:05:39.199 --> 00:05:42.700
Oh, it's a hide the hedgehog game.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:43.603
Bear, catch.

00:05:45.202 --> 00:05:46.035
(laughs)

00:05:46.035 --> 00:05:47.480
All right, go play with
your hedgehog, Bear.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.460
Thank you for the hedgehog, Bear loves it.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:50.714
I think, I think you...

00:05:50.714 --> 00:05:52.035
(loud snap)
(gasps)

00:05:52.035 --> 00:05:53.368
Ow!

00:05:53.368 --> 00:05:55.853
(screaming)

00:05:55.853 --> 00:05:57.833
I sliced my finger open!

00:05:58.970 --> 00:05:59.810
- [Dan] Should we get a doctor?

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:03.130
- I want you to pause
the camera Dan, please.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.980
- [Man] A few moments layer.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.519
- Look, this is my own therapy dog.

00:06:06.519 --> 00:06:07.352
(paper rustling)

00:06:07.352 --> 00:06:10.470
It is a Connoisseur Tea Kit.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.060
Ooh, some green tea.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.780
Matcha.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.797
I'm not gonna even try to pronounce that.

00:06:16.797 --> 00:06:20.527
"Hey Dr. Mike, I'm happy to
share a love of tea with you.

00:06:20.527 --> 00:06:22.820
"Hopefully these are new
editions to your cupboard."

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:25.110
Wow that's so cool, I'm
excited to try these.

